Design a 32-bit signed multiplier block that computes a specific multiplication operation using bit shifts and additions. The input value is manipulated through a series of shifts (left by 6, 7, and 8 bits) to derive intermediate values, which are then combined through addition and subtraction to achieve the final output. The output represents the result of a customized multiplication process, effectively combining shifted versions of the input to arrive at the end value.
