description:
Design a 4-bit binary counter that increments on each rising edge of the clock signal. The counter resets to zero when the reset input is activated. It counts from 0 to 7 and wraps back to 0 upon reaching the value of 7, ensuring it operates as a modulo-8 counter. The output is represented on a 4-bit wide output signal that reflects the current count value.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input reset,
  output reg [3:0] count
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input reset,
  output reg [3:0] count
);reg [3:0] temp_count;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (reset) begin
    temp_count <= 4'b0000;
  end
  else begin
    if (temp_count == 4'b0111) begin
      temp_count <= 4'b0000;
    end
    else begin
      temp_count <= temp_count + 1;
    end
  end
end

assign count = temp_count;

endmodule

