Design a circuit that calculates the magnitude of a 4-bit input number and outputs a 3-bit representation of its magnitude. The module uses combinational logic to map specific input ranges to corresponding output values. Each group of input values is assigned a unique output based on their magnitude, effectively categorizing the 4-bit input into levels from 0 to 7 (in binary: 000 to 111) based on predefined ranges.
