description:
Design a Fibonacci sequence generator that computes Fibonacci numbers in an 8-bit output format. On a reset signal, it initializes the sequence with the first number, 1. On each clock cycle, the module uses a state machine to control progress through the Fibonacci sequence; it shifts the current values, adds them together in a specific control sequence, and updates the output with the latest Fibonacci number. The design effectively implements a finite state machine (FSM) to manage state transitions and arithmetic operations required for generating the sequence.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [7:0] fib
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [7:0] fib
);reg [7:0] shift_reg;
reg [1:0] control;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    if (reset) begin
        shift_reg <= 2'b01;
        control <= 2'b00;
        fib <= 8'b00000001;
    end else begin
        case (control)
            2'b00: begin
                shift_reg <= {shift_reg[6:0], shift_reg[7]};
                control <= 2'b01;
            end
            2'b01: begin
                shift_reg <= {shift_reg[6:0], shift_reg[7]};
                control <= 2'b10;
            end
            2'b10: begin
                shift_reg <= shift_reg + {shift_reg[6:0], shift_reg[7]};
                control <= 2'b00;
                fib <= shift_reg;
            end
        endcase
    end
end

endmodule

