description:
Design a circuit that produces a high output Y based on specific conditions of the six input signals. The output Y will be high (1) when either both A1 and A2 are high while both B1 and B2 are low, or both A1 and A2 are low while both B1 and B2 are high, or when C1 is high. Otherwise, the output will be low (0). This module can be seen as implementing a form of logic function or a small combinational logic unit.
module top_module(
    input A1, A2, B1, B2, C1, VPB, VPWR, VGND, VNB, 
    output Y
);

code:
module top_module(
    input A1, A2, B1, B2, C1, VPB, VPWR, VGND, VNB, 
    output Y
);assign Y = ((A1 & A2 & ~B1 & ~B2) | (~A1 & ~A2 & B1 & B2) | C1) ? 1'b1 : 1'b0;

endmodule

